<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout xml:id="dailyprep312">
<title>Daily Prep</title>

  <!-- <page>
    <p workspace="1in">
      A first paragraph with some space for notes below it.
    </p>

  </page> -->

  <page>
    
  <p>The best way to fully benefit from our class time together is to be reasonably prepared for class.  To that end, each section of the text includes a Preview Activity.  These activities are connected questions that prepare you for what is coming in a given section through recall of key ideas of previous mathematics you have learned.  They are often constructive and highlight a core idea of the section.    
  </p>
  


  <p>These assignments are intended to be formative in nature.  As such, the grading rubric in <xref ref="DailyPrep312Rubric"/> will be utilized.   
  </p>

  <table xml:id="DailyPrep312Rubric" >
<title>Daily Prep Grading Rubric</title>
<tabular halign="center" bottom="minor" top="minor">
<row header="no" bottom="medium" top="medium">
<cell> <alert>Score</alert> </cell>
<cell> <alert>Description</alert> </cell>
</row>

<row>
<cell> 4 </cell> 
<cell> All questions thoughtfully addressed with sufficient justifications provided. </cell>     
</row>

<row>
<cell> 3 </cell>  
<cell> More than 90% complete, but lacking key justifications </cell>  
</row>

<row>
<cell> 2 </cell> 
<cell> Submission looks to be a last-minute thought submitted with few if any explanations </cell>  
</row>

<row>
<cell> 1 </cell> 
<cell> Less than half of what was requested was submitted; little thought put into work </cell>   
</row>

<row>
<cell> 0 </cell> 
<cell> No submission </cell> 
</row>

</tabular>
</table>

 </page> 

 <page> 

    <p>Based on the calendar found in <xref ref="schedule-dailyprep-table"/>, please submit your attempts to respond to the questions in each Preview Activity.  <alert>Submissions will be limited to a single file.  Please convert that single file to PDF before submission to D2L Brightspace.</alert>
  </p>

  <p>
    In <xref ref="schedule-dailyprep-table"/> are deadlines for the daily prep assignments to be uploaded to D2L for grading.  
  </p>

